},"comments":7,"created_at":"2026-04-16T12:15:28Z","updated_at":"2026-04-20T14:23:54Z","closed_at":"2026-04-20T14:23:54Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproductible in 4.7.dev [34777ad] and after\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Forward +\n\n### Issue description\n\nAdding preview breakpoints to a text shader can lead to crashes. For example:\n\nIf you have a loop that does something like:\n```\n1 - float x = 0.0;\n2 - while(x < 0.5) {\n3 -  float temp = x + 0.1;\n4 -  x += 0.1\n5 - }\n```\n\nPlacing a breakpoint on line 4 is okay, but placing a breakpoint on line 3 creates an infinite loop because the line `x += 0.1` gets removed.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a shader containing a while loop. For example:\n```\n...\nvoid fragment() {\n  ...\n  float x = 0.0;\n  while (x < 0.5) {\n    float temp = x + 0.1;\n    x += 0.1;\n  }\n}\n...\n```\n\n- Place a breakpoint on line 4 - see that it is okay\n- Place a breakpoint on line 3 - see that it creates an infinite loop because the line `x += 0.1` gets removed.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26783781/mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https: